Language: en-GB
Description: Tools for fitting and interrogating Reduced-Rank Generalised Dissimilarity Models (RRGDM). RRGDM extends
    classic Generalised Dissimilarity Models by embedding sites in a low-dimensional
    latent space via 'TMB' (Template Model Builder). Environmental predictors, random
    effects, and effects on dispersion can all be specified directly on the latent
    positions rather than on pairwise distances, unifying ordination and
    dissimilarity regression within a single framework. Includes
    tools for model fitting, prediction, inference on environmental loadings and
    dispersion effects, goodness-of-fit assessment, and visualisation of model-based ordination.
